winehaiku.drv: a sound driver on Haiku's Media Kit (render only; no capture, no MIDI).

One BSoundPlayer per stream, connected to the system mixer, which converts the
stream's own format (8/16/32-bit PCM, 32-bit float; any rate, 1-8 channels).
The player pulls from the stream's ring buffer on a Media Kit thread, as
winecoreaudio's render callback does. The Media Kit is C++ and makedep builds no
C++: haiku_player.cpp is compiled outside Wine's make (scripts/build-wine.sh, into
a static library) and given to configure in HAIKU_AUDIO_LIBS. mmdevapi tries
"haiku" first.

